  "step_3": "The decision reason emphasizes identifying a favorable outcome and choosing the lottery with the higher probability of achieving it, treating outcome differences as negligible. In this case, the favorable outcome is 'no loss' (0 Euros), which only Lottery A offers, with 50% probability. The individual’s reasoning explicitly centers on wanting to 'keep the chance of no loss,' which directly aligns with prioritizing the probability of achieving a favorable outcome. The comparison between the lotteries based on the chance to avoid loss matches the rule of the decision reason. Therefore, both the relevant information (probability of favorable outcome) and the justification (preserving a chance to avoid loss) align closely with the decision reason. The verbal report strongly reflects the use of this reason, even if not articulated in identical terms.",
